- **ML eval-set contamination discovered + v7 real-world recall problem -- 2026-07-07 (ADVANCED 2026-07-10: the "clean split first" plan was executed and v8 measured -- see the "v8 held-out result DONE 2026-07-10" entry above)** --
  Working session toward a v8 detector retrain. The headline discovery
  is a **data-leakage / evaluation-contamination bug** that invalidates
  the v7 mAP numbers as generalization evidence, plus solid evidence
  that v7 has a real **recall** problem that a threshold change will not
  fix. Nothing was retrained or committed; this is a findings + next-steps
  log so the next session can resume without re-deriving all of it.

  **1. Eval-set contamination (the blocker).**
  - Every PDF v7 has ever been scored on -- the 5 "held-out"
    (`generic3`, `K`, `makayla1`, `D`, `Electrical_Takeoff_page7`) AND
    the other 17 in `~/Documents/pdfToScan/` -- has pages in v7's
    training set. Verified directly: the v6 training images
    (`~/Documents/TableAnnotations/v6/images/real__*`) were built from
    `~/Documents/TableAnnotations/images/` (48 annotated source PNGs),
    and that source folder contains pages from all 22 pdfToScan PDFs
    (e.g. `...-generic3_page001.png`, `...-K_page001.png`,
    `...-D_page001.png`, 10x `derek2_page*`, 9-10x `derekfirst_page*`).
    For the single-page PDFs the exact trained page IS the page the
    eval renders.
  - Therefore the v7 SUMMARY's claim ("All five PDFs are NOT in
    `images/`, so this is a clean held-out evaluation") is **false**,
    and both v7's 0.83 (5-PDF) and tonight's 0.74 (22-PDF) are
    training-set scores. **True held-out generalization is currently
    unknown.**
  - Consequence for v8: a retrain cannot be validly measured against
    these PDFs. A clean train/test split must be established FIRST.

  **2. v7 under-detects badly even on trained data (recall problem).**
  Ran v7 (`models_v7/best`, conf 0.5, IoU 0.5) vs the heuristic
  (ground truth) on all 22 pdfToScan PDFs; results in
  `~/Documents/TableAnnotations/baselines/v7_expanded_2026-07-07/`
  (NOT locked -- contaminated, keep for reference only). Full-set
  avg mAP@0.5 ~= 0.74. The error mode is unambiguous and consistent:
  **false negatives dominate; precision is near-perfect** (exactly ONE
  false positive across all 22 PDFs, on `H`). Worst cases are dense /
  specific-style sheets: `derek2` 40 GT -> 13 pred (recall 0.25),
  `derekfirst` 23 -> 9 (0.35), `generic2` 5 -> 4 (0.40 -> mAP 0.20),
  `A` 7 -> 4 (0.43). Note recall does NOT track raw panel count:
  `O` (29 panels) scored recall 0.97 and `L` (12) 1.00, while
  `derek2` (40) cratered -- so the misses concentrate on a *style*
  of sheet (the "derek"-style drawings, `generic2`, `A`), likely
  small / unusually-formatted panels, not density per se.

  **3. Threshold tuning does NOT fix it (structural, needs retrain).**
  Confidence sweep on Paperspace GPU (partial -- timed out at 900s
  after `generic2` all + `A` at 0.5/0.3/0.2; `C`/`derek2` sweep points
  did not run), results in
  `~/Documents/TableAnnotations/baselines/v7_confsweep_2026-07-07/`:
  - `generic2`: recall **flat at 0.40** across conf 0.5 -> 0.3 -> 0.2
    -> 0.1; lowering conf only added false positives (precision
    0.50 -> 0.40), recovered zero missed panels.
  - `A`: recall 0.43 (c0.5) -> 0.57 (c0.3, c0.2) then plateaus; one
    extra true panel recovered but still far short of the 7 GT.
  Conclusion: the missed panels are not low-confidence proposals being
  thresholded out -- the model isn't proposing them at all. A v8
  **retrain targeting recall** is required; a conf change is not a fix.

  **4. Clean (not-in-training) PDFs available for a real held-out set.**
  `~/Documents/Diagrams/` contains PDFs NOT in the training set:
  `chucksmall.pdf`, `ELECTRICAL SET (Mark Up).pdf` (+ its
  `..._electrical_filtered.pdf` variant), and `Panels_Example.pdf`.
  The rest of that folder (`generic2/3`, `good_tester_combo`,
  `makayla1/2`, `NoAmps`) ARE in training. Since the heuristic is
  ground truth (see STANDING DECISION entry above), any new PDF can be
  auto-labeled for both training and eval without manual annotation --
  so building a bigger clean test set is cheap.

  **5. Recommended plan for the next session (NOT yet approved by
  Marco -- he skipped the direction question and said "log these
  issues, continue tomorrow"):**
  1. **Establish a clean train/test split.** Reserve a set of PDFs
     (start with the `Diagrams/` clean ones + collect more real
     sheets, especially "derek"-style / small-panel / dense grids)
     used ONLY for eval, never for training.
  2. **Re-baseline v7 honestly** on that clean set to get a real
     generalization number (expect it below 0.74).
  3. **Then** plan/run the v8 recall retrain (heuristic-auto-labeled
     training data biased toward the failing sheet styles), measured
     only on the clean held-out set, compared head-to-head vs the
     locked v7.
  - Open decision Marco still needs to make: clean-split-first
    (recommended) vs gather-more-data-first vs retrain-now-accept-caveat.

