- **OCR pipeline advanced to APIv12 + RulesEngine input hardening -- LANDED 2026-07-03 (merge `04a2361`)** --
  A `TOOL_Debug_MaxUserTesting` -> `TOOL_DEVELOPMENT_V3_MS` merge advanced
  the production OCR pipeline and added a defense-in-depth layer so junk/
  ambiguous OCR can no longer manufacture a wrong-but-plausible quoteable
  BOM. This is committed and on `origin/TOOL_DEVELOPMENT_V3_MS`; the docs
  (`architecture.mdc`, `file-locations.mdc`, `data-structures.mdc`) were
  synced in the same session. What changed:
  - **`uplink_server.py` now imports `OcrLibrary.BreakerTableParserAPIv12`**
    (was APIv11); `API_VERSION = "API_12"`. New file
    `OcrLibrary/BreakerTableParserAPIv12.py` (746 lines). APIv11 is retained
    for comparison. Per the versioned-module convention, always confirm the
    active version from the imports at the top of `uplink_server.py`.
  - **New RulesEngine input sanitizer** `_rules_safe_components()` (plus
    helper `_is_problem_component_for_rules()`) in `uplink_server.py`. It is
    applied on **all three** rules entry points -- `_process_job()`,
    `vm_rerun_rules_with_panel_edit()`, and
    `vm_rerun_rules_with_global_defaults()` -- and returns a RulesEngine-only
    copy. The saved `result.json` components still keep the raw/editable OCR
    evidence; only the rules input is sanitized. Problem panels (`_skipped`
    or non-empty `panelStatus`) are fully suppressed for rules (quote-driving
    attrs nulled, `attrs.breaker_data_suppressed` +
    `attrs.breaker_suppression_reason` set). Clean panels are validated/
    snapped: bus & main amps 100-1200 ending in 0/5; voltage in
    {120,208,240,480,600}; intRating in the standard AIC set; spaces snapped
    to standard even counts (16->18, 40->42, ...) and capped at 84; trim in
    {SURFACE,FLUSH} (forced None for NEMA3R); breakers filtered to amps
    15-1200, poles 1/2/3, not exceeding the panel's main/bus limit.
  - **`PanelHeaderParserV11` gained two guards**:
    `_looks_like_aic_or_ka_text()` (blocks `65k`, `65KA`, `65KAIC`, `AIC: 65`,
    `65,000 A`, "Available Fault Current", etc.) and
    `_looks_like_non_amp_context_text()` (blocks numeric location/source
    metadata like `Location: ELECTRICAL 123`, `Fed From: MDP-1`,
    `Serving RTU-3`, while deliberately NOT blocking legit BUS/MAIN/MCB
    rating text). These are wired into every BUS/MAIN amp extraction path so
    such text is never read as amps.
  - **`_merge_component_from_btp()` hardening**: it now reads the header
    parser's `headerValidationMissing` list and nulls `amperage`/`voltage`/
    `mainBreakerAmperage` when the field was flagged missing or is out of the
    valid range; parser-flagged panels (`panelStatus`) get `_skipped=True`
    and a `reason`.
  - **Manual-edit flow (`vm_rerun_rules_with_panel_edit`)** now clears more
    stale status on edit: `panelStatus`, `panelNote`, `specialHeaderType`,
    `_skipped`, `reason`, and the `attrs` keys `breaker_data_suppressed`,
    `breaker_suppression_reason`, `headerValidationStatus`,
    `headerValidationMissing`. A user-corrected panel is therefore re-judged
    purely from the edited attrs + a fresh rules rerun, instead of inheriting
    the original parser's problem flags.
  - **Guidance for future work**: when adding a new quote-driving attribute,
    extend `_rules_safe_components()` (not just the parser) so an unvalidated
    value can't leak into the rules engine. The commit message on `6847d9c`
    also references a `BreakerTableParserAPIv12` switch tied to
    "preserve breakers so only panel attrs need editing to save a panel";
    the amps-hardening is `944ca14`.

